+# Filtering the Veterinarian Directory by Specialty Is In Scope; a Page Control Is Not
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined search for pets, visits, and veterinarians, leaving only owners searchable. It was derived from observed absence in the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey, so whether it was deliberate stayed unknown. A request to narrow the veterinarian directory to one specialty lands squarely on that row.
+
+The row conflates two capabilities. One is free-text search over an entity, which is what owner search demonstrates. The other is narrowing a list by an attribute that list already displays. The owner decided the boundary between them on 2026-09-09, and decided at the same time that this round adds no visible control.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Read NG-9 as written and decline the filter.** Rejected: the row's rationale is about repeating paged prefix search, which a whole-name filter does not repeat.
+2. **Drop NG-9.** Rejected: free-text veterinarian search remains declined, and dropping the row would reopen it by implication.
+3. **Narrow NG-9 to free-text search, and record the absent control as its own row** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 covers free-text search only. Narrowing a directory by an attribute it already shows is in scope, which is what `REQ-VET-003` states for the veterinarian directory.
+
+NG-10 records the second half of the decision: neither form of the directory gains a form, dropdown, or other page control in this round. The filter is a request contract. A visible control comes only as a follow-up request.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation as a decided row; free-text veterinarian search stays declined.
+- A later request to filter another list by a displayed attribute is in scope without reopening NG-9.
+- The filter is reachable only by composing a request, so nobody browsing the pages can discover it.
+- Narrowing NG-10 later is a recorded owner decision with its own non-goal ADR, per the table's convention.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9, NG-10
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row and the new row.
+- [PRD REQ-VET-003](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the capability the narrowing admits.
